id: pm-fqlocp
title: "GH-1183: Windows nightly event-index lock acquisition and fallback publication are nondeterministic"
description: "Nightly Validation run 33734934714 on main 41200e76b failed twice on Windows Node 24: scale workspace SDK writes received EPERM while opening the history-event-index lock, and the unlocked-fallback append regression observed an index file that should have remained unpublished. Treat Windows lock denial consistently with contention, isolate test hooks, and preserve the rule that an unlocked fallback append can never publish a size-certified incomplete index."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:history","area:tests",ci,locks,windows
created_at: "2026-09-03T09:11:33.408Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-03T09:59:26.688Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-03T09:55:35.701Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-03T09:55:35.701Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: The Windows Node 24 full suite passes repeatedly; scale direct/SDK layouts remain byte-identical; EPERM contention is bounded and recoverable; an unlocked fallback append invalidates or withholds the event index; focused lock/event-index tests and exact coverage pass.
parent: pm-u9d0
severity: high
environment: "GitHub Actions windows-latest, Node 24, run 33734934714 at main 41200e76b"
repro_steps: Run the full nightly suite on Windows; observe EPERM opening locks/history-event-index.lock in scale-workspace equivalence and an unexpectedly present runtime history-event-index after the forced unlocked fallback append.
resolution: Lock creation now retries Windows delete-pending errors only with filesystem contention evidence; event-index fallback tests assert committed invalidation rather than POSIX-only unlink; typed lineage and exact regression coverage are recorded.
expected_result: "Windows Node 24 scale SDK writes tolerate bounded delete-pending contention without concealing permissions, and unlocked fallback appends never expose an incomplete derived index."
actual_result: "Focused 98-test regression suite, complete 8,323-test exact coverage, tracker-context quality, packed npx/bunx, and fresh installed SDK/CLI lifecycle acceptance all pass."
affected_version: 2026.9.3
component: history event index and cross-platform lock
regression: true
