comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-03T09:11:33.408Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: all-status searches for EPERM history-event-index Windows lock, unlocked fallback append incomplete index, and Nightly Validation Windows found no item owning this combined event-index regression. pm-tgq6 owns an older stale-cleanup mock-path flake, pm-zwib owns stale-lock takeover safety, and pm-801d owns the broader derived-index roadmap; this item preserves the distinct GH-1183 failure evidence."
  "2026-09-03T09:11:59.050Z","harness:codex","Implementation start: the exact nightly log shows two independent retry-stable failures on main 41200e76b: EPERM opening locks/history-event-index.lock during scale SDK history appends, and a forced unlocked-fallback append leaving runtime/history-event-index.json present. I will preserve cross-platform lock semantics and the fail-closed derived-index publication invariant, then verify with focused, full exact-coverage, packed, and Windows CI evidence."
  "2026-09-03T09:33:38.424Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: Windows delete-pending EPERM, EACCES, and EBUSY create failures are retryable only when an existing lock or writable parent proves contention; genuine directory permission failures remain fatal. Event-index fallback coverage now asserts the portable public invariant that a committed invalidation marker makes the index unqueryable even when Windows keeps an open SQLite file physically present. Focused lock, index, and scale equivalence suite passed 98 tests."
  "2026-09-03T09:55:35.162Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: exact full suite passed 600 files and 8,323 tests at 100% statements (61,477/61,477), branches (46,551/46,551), functions (12,799/12,799), and lines (59,157/59,157). Packed npx and bunx smoke passed version 2026.9.3 across 13 packages. Fresh temporary installed-package acceptance created, claimed, updated, read four immutable history events, closed, released, health-checked, and validated pm-ia4g entirely through the public CLI and @unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/runtime."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-03T09:33:38.900Z","harness:codex","Cross-platform derived-cache correctness must depend on committed invalidation and content-size evidence, not successful physical unlink. Windows exclusive-create errors should be reclassified as contention only with filesystem evidence so retry tolerance cannot conceal genuine permissions."
